Subject: [PATCH 27/27] kosmickrisp: KK_MSL_CANON_KEY (default off): canonical override keys, macOS/GPU independent

KK's generated MSL (so every KK_MSL_OVERRIDE_DIR key) depends on the OS and the
GPU family (workarounds resolved on macOS 27, M5+ only workarounds, texture
lowering by family). With KK_MSL_CANON_KEY=1 every shader also gets the key of
the text a macOS 26 / Apple GPU family 9 machine writes: a second, text-only
translation of cloned NIR with the canonical workaround set / family / OS
(thread-local), none on that machine class itself. Override lookup tries the
real key, then the canonical key, so tables made on that class match
unchanged. The `seen` log line carries canon=<key>. The keys are stored as an
optional shader-binary trailer (old caches stay valid, codegen unchanged);
the pipeline cache UUID only changes where the keys can differ and the switch is
on. Only plain VS/FS/compute pipelines get the second translation.

